/-!
# Flat pullback preserves torsion freeness for an invertible ideal

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a flat morphism of ringed spaces whose structure-sheaf stalks are local
rings, let `I ⊆ 𝒪_Y` be an invertible ideal sheaf and let `F` be an `I`-torsion-free sheaf of
`𝒪_Y`-modules.  This file proves that `f^*F` is `f^*I`-torsion-free, and records the degreewise
consequence for a cochain complex of `I`-torsion-free modules.

`η` of a complex needs torsion freeness of its terms to be formed at all, so the comparisons of
décalages under a pullback, `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.pullbackEtaMap` and
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.pullbackDerivedEtaMap`, take the torsion freeness of the pulled-back
complex as a hypothesis; for flat `f` it is supplied by the results here.

## Main results

* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isIdealTorsionFree_pullback_of_isFlat`: **flat pullback preserves
  `I`-torsion freeness**, `F[I] = 0` implies `(f^*F)[f^*I] = 0`.
* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isIdealTorsionFree_pullbackComplex_of_isFlat`: the same degreewise
  for a cochain complex.

## Implementation notes

The argument runs through the stalkwise characterization of Stacks 0GT5, clause 5 of
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.idealTorsionFree_tfae`: on both spaces the ideal sheaf is invertible, hence
finite locally free of rank one (Stacks 0B8M, in the form
`Stacks.RingedSpace.isInvertible_iff_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one`, which is where the
hypothesis on the stalks is spent), so the tag applies on `Y` and on `X` and the content is the
passage between the two stalkwise statements.

Fix `x : X` and a generator `g` of the stalk ideal `(f^*I)_x ⊆ 𝒪_{X,x}`.  Since `I` is
invertible it is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor
(`Stacks.IdealTorsion.isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_of_isInvertible`), so near `f x` there is a
section of `I` generating it, and the germ `t` of its ambient section generates the stalk ideal
`I_{f x}`.  Two facts about `t` finish the proof.  Its image in `𝒪_{X,x}` lies in the stalk
ideal of `f^*I` — the pullback-unit image of the generating section represents it, by
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.idealSection_pullbackIdealIncl` and the germ formula for a stalk map —
hence is a multiple of `g`, and so regularity of the image implies regularity of `g`.  And the
image is regular on the stalk of `f^*F` because `t` is regular on the stalk of `F`, by Stacks
0098 in the form `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.exists_modulePullbackStalkLinearEquiv`: the stalk
of `f^*F` at `x` is `𝒪_{X,x} ⊗_{𝒪_{Y,f x}} F_{f x}`, flatness of `f` makes `𝒪_{X,x}` a flat
`𝒪_{Y,f x}`-algebra, and base change along a flat algebra preserves regularity
(`IsSMulRegular.of_flat_of_isBaseChange`).

Two module structures on the stalk of a sheaf of modules are in play: the one Mathlib puts on a
colimit of modules, which is the one the stalk formula for a pullback is stated over, and the one
built from germ representatives, which is the one the stalkwise characterization is stated over.
They are equal (`Stacks.IdealTorsion.stalkModule_eq`) but not definitionally, so the base-change
step is proved in a section where the Mathlib structure has the higher instance priority and the
equality is crossed by `isSMulRegular_congr_module` at each end.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0098](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0098)
-/

@[expose] public section

attribute [local instance_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafedSpace.sheaf Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite

open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction (opensMap)

open Stacks.RingedSpace (pullbackFunctor pullbackUnit)

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace (O ringStalk ringGerm grpStalk stalkModule)

universe u

namespace Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta

/-! ### Transporting regularity -/

/-- The scalar action underlying a module structure, read as a function of that structure.  This
is what lets an equality of module structures be transported through `IsSMulRegular`, whose
scalar action is an instance argument. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def moduleSMul {R M : Type u} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    (i : Module R M) : SMul R M :=
  letI : Module R M := i
  inferInstance

/-- Regularity of a scalar depends on a module structure only through its value, so it
transports along an equality of module structures. -/
private theorem isSMulRegular_congr_module {R M : Type u} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    {i₁ i₂ : Module R M} (h : i₁ = i₂) (r : R)
    (hr : @IsSMulRegular R M (moduleSMul i₁) r) : @IsSMulRegular R M (moduleSMul i₂) r :=
  h ▸ hr

/-- **Base change along a flat algebra preserves regularity.** A scalar regular on `M` stays
regular, as its image, on `S ⊗_R M` when `S` is a flat `R`-algebra: the tensor product is the
base change of `M`, and `IsSMulRegular.of_flat_of_isBaseChange` applies. -/
private theorem isSMulRegular_tensorProduct {R S M : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [Module.Flat R S] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {t : R}
    (h : IsSMulRegular M t) : IsSMulRegular (TensorProduct R S M) (algebraMap R S t) :=
  h.of_flat_of_isBaseChange (TensorProduct.isBaseChange R M S)

/-- A scalar is regular as soon as one of its multiples is: if `c = r * g` acts injectively then
so does `g`, since `c • m = r • g • m`. -/
private theorem isSMulRegular_of_mul {R M : Type u} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    {g r c : R} (hc : c = r * g) (h : IsSMulRegular M c) : IsSMulRegular M g :=
  (hc ▸ h).of_mul

/-! ### The germ of a generating section generates the stalk ideal -/

/-- **The germ of a generating section of the ideal generates the stalk ideal.** Every element of
the stalk ideal is the germ of the ambient section of some local section of the ideal; on the
intersection with the generating section's open that section is a multiple of the generator, and
germs turn the multiple into a multiple in the stalk.

This is the sectionwise-to-stalkwise step of Stacks 0GT5. -/
private theorem generatesStalkIdeal_germ (Z : RingedSpace.{u})
    {I : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Z.sheaf)}
    (i : I ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheaf Z.sheaf)) (U : Opens Z)
    (a : I.val.obj (op U)) (hgen : GeneratesIdealOn Z U a) (z : Z) (hzU : z ∈ U) :
    GeneratesStalkIdeal Z i z (ringGerm Z z U hzU (idealSection Z i (op U) a)) := by
  refine ⟨⟨U, hzU, a, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  intro c hc
  obtain ⟨V, hzV, b, hb⟩ := hc
  set W : Opens Z := V ⊓ U
  have hzW : z ∈ W := ⟨hzV, hzU⟩
  set bW : I.val.obj (op W) := (I.val.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op).hom b with hbW
  set aW : I.val.obj (op W) := (I.val.map (homOfLE inf_le_right).op).hom a with haW
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hgen W inf_le_right bW
  let r' : (O Z).obj (op W) := r
  refine ⟨ringGerm Z z W hzW r, ?_⟩
  have hsmul : idealSection Z i (op W) bW = r' * idealSection Z i (op W) aW := by
    have hr' : bW = r' • aW := hr
    rw [hr']
    show (i.val.app (op W)).hom (r' • aW) = _
    rw [map_smul]
    rfl
  calc c = ringGerm Z z V hzV (idealSection Z i (op V) b) := hb.symm
    _ = ringGerm Z z W hzW (idealSection Z i (op W) bW) := by
        rw [hbW, Stacks.IdealTorsion.idealSection_naturality Z i (homOfLE inf_le_left).op b]
        simp [ringGerm, O]
    _ = ringGerm Z z W hzW r' * ringGerm Z z W hzW (idealSection Z i (op W) aW) := by
        rw [hsmul, map_mul]
    _ = ringGerm Z z W hzW r * ringGerm Z z U hzU (idealSection Z i (op U) a) := by
        congr 1
        rw [haW, Stacks.IdealTorsion.idealSection_naturality Z i (homOfLE inf_le_right).op a]
        simp [ringGerm, O]

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- **The image of a germ of the ideal lies in the stalk ideal of the pullback.** The
pullback-unit image of a section `a` of `I` over `U` is a section of `f^*I` over `f^{-1}U` whose
ambient section is `f^♯` of the ambient section of `a`
(`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.idealSection_pullbackIdealIncl`); its germ at `x` is therefore the
image under the stalk map of the germ of the ambient section of `a` at `f x`. -/
private theorem stalkMap_germ_idealSection_mem_stalkIdeal
    (I : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf))
    (ι : I ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheaf Y.sheaf))
    (x : X) (U : Opens Y) (hyU : f.hom.base x ∈ U) (a : I.val.obj (op U)) :
    (f.hom.stalkMap x) (ringGerm Y (f.hom.base x) U hyU (idealSection Y ι (op U) a))
      ∈ stalkIdeal X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) x :=
  have hx : x ∈ (opensMap f).obj U := hyU
  ⟨(opensMap f).obj U, hx, pullbackUnit f I (op U) a,
    (congrArg (ringGerm X x ((opensMap f).obj U) hx)
        (idealSection_pullbackIdealIncl f I ι (op U) a)).trans
      (AlgebraicGeometry.PresheafedSpace.stalkMap_germ_apply f.hom U x hyU
        (idealSection Y ι (op U) a)).symm⟩

/-! ### Regularity on the stalk of a flat pullback -/

section

/- The stalk formula for a pullback of sheaves of modules is stated over Mathlib's module
structure on a colimit of modules, whereas `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace`
installs the germ-representative structure as a global instance of the same type.  The two are
equal but not definitionally so; raising the priority of the former makes it the one the
statement below is written over, and `isSMulRegular_congr_module` crosses the equality at the
two ends. -/
attribute [local instance 20000]
  PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier

/-- **A scalar regular on a stalk of `F` has a regular image on the corresponding stalk of
`f^*F`, for flat `f`.** By Stacks 0098 the stalk of `f^*F` at `x` is the base change
`𝒪_{X,x} ⊗_{𝒪_{Y,f x}} F_{f x}`, flatness of `f` says exactly that `𝒪_{X,x}` is a flat
`𝒪_{Y,f x}`-algebra, and base change along a flat algebra preserves regularity.

Both stalks carry Mathlib's module structure here; see the note above the section. -/
private theorem isSMulRegular_stalk_pullback (hf : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlat f)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf)) (x : X)
    (t : ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x))
    (hreg : IsSMulRegular (grpStalk Y F.val (f.hom.base x)) t) :
    IsSMulRegular (grpStalk X ((pullbackFunctor f).obj F).val x) ((f.hom.stalkMap x) t) := by
  let : Algebra (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ringStalk X x) :=
    (f.hom.stalkMap x).hom.toAlgebra
  have hflat : Module.Flat (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ringStalk X x) := hf x
  obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.exists_modulePullbackStalkLinearEquiv f F x
  have htens := isSMulRegular_tensorProduct (S := ringStalk X x) hreg
  have halg : (algebraMap (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ringStalk X x)) t
      = (f.hom.stalkMap x) t := rfl
  rw [halg] at htens
  intro m n hmn
  exact e.injective (htens (by simpa only [map_smul] using congrArg e hmn))

end

/-! ### Torsion freeness of a flat pullback -/

variable (I : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf))
  (ι : I ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheaf Y.sheaf)) [Mono ι]

/-- **The stalkwise characterization of torsion freeness passes to a flat pullback.** A generator
`g` of the stalk ideal of `f^*I` at `x` divides the image of the germ `t` of a local generator of
`I` near `f x`, which exists because an invertible ideal sheaf on a ringed space with local
stalks is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor; that image is regular on the stalk of `f^*F` by
flat base change, hence so is `g`. -/
private theorem isStalkwiseGeneratorRegular_pullback (hf : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlat f)
    [hI : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj (structureSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
    [∀ y : Y, IsLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y)]
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf))
    (hst : IsStalkwiseGeneratorRegular Y ι F) :
    IsStalkwiseGeneratorRegular X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) ((pullbackFunctor f).obj F) := by
  intro x g hg
  obtain ⟨U, hyU, a, hgen, -⟩ :=
    isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_of_isInvertible Y ι hI (f.hom.base x)
  set t := ringGerm Y (f.hom.base x) U hyU (idealSection Y ι (op U) a)
  have hregY := isSMulRegular_congr_module
    (stalkModule_eq Y F.val (f.hom.base x)).symm t
    (hst (f.hom.base x) t (generatesStalkIdeal_germ Y ι U a hgen (f.hom.base x) hyU))
  have hregX := isSMulRegular_congr_module
    (stalkModule_eq X ((pullbackFunctor f).obj F).val x) ((f.hom.stalkMap x) t)
    (isSMulRegular_stalk_pullback f hf F x t hregY)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hg.2 _ (stalkMap_germ_idealSection_mem_stalkIdeal f I ι x U hyU a)
  exact isSMulRegular_of_mul hr hregX

/-- **Flat pullback preserves torsion freeness for an invertible ideal.** If `F` has no
`I`-torsion then `f^*F` has no `f^*I`-torsion, for a flat morphism `f` of ringed spaces whose
structure-sheaf stalks are local rings.

Both ideal sheaves are invertible, hence finite locally free of rank one, so the stalkwise
clause 5 of Stacks 0GT5 is available on `Y` and on `X`; the content is
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isStalkwiseGeneratorRegular_pullback`, the passage between the two
stalkwise statements. -/
theorem isIdealTorsionFree_pullback_of_isFlat (hf : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlat f)
    [hI : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj (structureSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
    [Mono (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)]
    [∀ x : X, IsLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x)]
    [∀ y : Y, IsLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y)]
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf))
    (hF : IsIdealTorsionFree Y ι F) :
    IsIdealTorsionFree X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) ((pullbackFunctor f).obj F) :=
  have hY : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      (C := Opens Y) (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology Y) I 1 :=
    (Stacks.RingedSpace.isInvertible_iff_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one Y I).1 hI
  have hX : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      (C := Opens X) (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) ((pullbackFunctor f).obj I) 1 :=
    (Stacks.RingedSpace.isInvertible_iff_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one X
      ((pullbackFunctor f).obj I)).1 (isInvertible_pullbackIdeal f I (h := hI))
  ((@idealTorsionFree_tfae X _ (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) (by assumption) hX
      ((pullbackFunctor f).obj F)).out 5 1).1
    (isStalkwiseGeneratorRegular_pullback f I ι hf F
      (((idealTorsionFree_tfae Y ι F).out 1 5).1 hF))

/-- **Flat pullback of a complex of torsion-free modules is termwise torsion free.** The
degreewise form of `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isIdealTorsionFree_pullback_of_isFlat`: the degree-`n`
term of the termwise pullback is the pullback of the degree-`n` term, so the previous theorem
applies degree by degree. -/
theorem isIdealTorsionFree_pullbackComplex_of_isFlat (hf : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlat f)
    [hI : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj (structureSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
    [Mono (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)]
    [∀ x : X, IsLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x)]
    [∀ y : Y, IsLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y)]
    (G : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf Y.sheaf)) ℤ)
    (hG : ∀ n : ℤ, IsIdealTorsionFree Y ι (G.X n)) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIdealTorsionFree X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) ((pullbackComplex f G).X n) :=
  isIdealTorsionFree_pullback_of_isFlat f I ι hf (G.X n) (hG n)

end Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta

end
